    "created_at": "2016-01-19T09:54:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-19T09:54:36Z",
    "body": "It's only used in the navigate algorithm for javascript URLs. I just found that javascript URLs are probably not correctly parsed by the URL standard, e.g., `<a href=javascript://x:x%0aalert(1)>test</a>` alerts 1 while that should really not parse at all per the current set of rules. So perhaps javascript URLs need to be special cased. Not sure if that should happen in the URL parser or in this algorithm yet.\n\nI guess I could file a separate bug on that though and fix this first...\n",
